{"Author":"mrbotic","Name":"Gearset Manager","InternalName":"GearsetManager","AssemblyVersion":"0.3.1.0","Description":"Your gearsets as a grid of job icons: one main set per unlocked job (its highest item level set), battle jobs then crafters then gatherers, with ultimate and spare sets underneath, labelled like "GNB · i790" and "GNB (FRU) · i730". The job you are wearing sits at the top. Click a set to equip it.

Re-arrange is a plan: drag jobs into order, mark sets to delete, and choose which missing jobs get a set made or skipped. Nothing changes in game until you press Apply, which deletes, makes the missing sets (weapon, soul crystal, recommended gear, saved) and renumbers. Undo puts the old order back.

/gsm opens the window. /gsm sort makes missing sets (if switched on) and applies the order to the game's list.","ApplicableVersion":"any","RepoUrl":"https://github.com/Marobotic/PfPresets","IconUrl":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Marobotic/PfPresets/main/repo/GearsetManager-icon.png","Tags":["gearset","armoury","sort","ultimate","ffxiv"],"DalamudApiLevel":15,"LoadRequiredState":0,"LoadSync":false,"CanUnloadAsync":false,"LoadPriority":0,"Punchline":"One set per job, in your order. Plan it, then apply.","Changelog":"First release. A new look: your sets as a grid of job icons with their item levels, the job you are wearing at the top, and a Re-arrange mode that plans everything before Apply. Making a set now skips jobs you have no weapon for, and makes room in a full armoury chest by moving items that are in no gearset to your bags. DMU counts as an ultimate.","AcceptsFeedback":false,"DownloadLinkInstall":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Marobotic/PfPresets/main/repo/GearsetManager.zip","DownloadLinkUpdate":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Marobotic/PfPresets/main/repo/GearsetManager.zip","DownloadLinkTesting":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Marobotic/PfPresets/main/repo/GearsetManager.zip"}

{"Author":"mrbotic","Name":"Gearset Manager","InternalName":"GearsetManager","AssemblyVersion":"0.3.1.0","Description":"Your gearsets as a grid of job icons: one main set per unlocked job (its highest item level set), battle jobs then crafters then gatherers, with ultimate and spare sets underneath, labelled like "GNB · i790" and "GNB (FRU) · i730". The job you are wearing sits at the top. Click a set to equip it.

